  {
   "id": "title",
   "label": "Errors and Trace Tables",
   "content": "<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Algorithm Design and Text Programming</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Errors and Trace Tables</h2><p>Year 9, 2.6</p></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Today:</strong> two kinds of error, and how to find them.</li><li><strong>You already know:</strong> FOR loops, IF, arrays and trace tables.</li><li><strong>Activities:</strong> trace a program to find its error, then fix programs and run them.</li></ul><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">A program runs but gives the wrong answer. Is that still an error?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Yes. A program can run and still be wrong. Today we learn to find both kinds of error.</p></div></details>"
  },
  {
   "id": "two-errors",
   "label": "Two Kinds of Error",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Two Kinds of Error</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: both programs should output 10. Which one will not run at all? Which one runs but gives the wrong answer?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p><strong>A</strong> will not run: OUTPT is not a keyword. That is a <strong>syntax error</strong>.</p><p><strong>B</strong> runs, but it multiplies, so Total stays 0. That is a <strong>logic error</strong>.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">A</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Total : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Total &larr; 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Count &larr; 1 TO 4</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &larr; Total + Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">OUTPT Total</div></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Syntax error:</strong> a line breaks the rules of the language.</li><li>The program <strong>will not run</strong>.</li></ul></div><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">B</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Total : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Total &larr; 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Count &larr; 1 TO 4</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &larr; Total * Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">OUTPUT Total</div></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Logic error:</strong> the program runs.</li><li>But the <strong>answer is wrong</strong>.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "kind-check",
   "label": "Check: Syntax or Logic?",
   "type": "multiple-choice",
   "containerId": "y9l26-kind-check",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Syntax or Logic?</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Which kind of error is harder to find? Why?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>A logic error. The program runs, so nothing tells you it is wrong. You have to check the answer.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Choose the kind of error in each line.</p><div id=\"y9l26-kind-check\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "prompt": "OUTPT Total",
     "options": [
      "Syntax error",
      "Logic error"
     ],
     "correct": 0,
     "explain": "OUTPUT is spelt wrong, so the program cannot run."
    },
    {
     "prompt": "FOR Count ← 1 TO 4 (the loop should run 5 times)",
     "options": [
      "Syntax error",
      "Logic error"
     ],
     "correct": 1,
     "explain": "The line follows the rules and runs, but the loop runs 4 times, not 5."
    },
    {
     "prompt": "DECLARE Total INTEGER",
     "options": [
      "Syntax error",
      "Logic error"
     ],
     "correct": 0,
     "explain": "The colon is missing, so the line breaks the rules."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trace-finds",
   "label": "A Trace Table Finds the Error",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">A Trace Table Finds the Error</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: this should output 10. What is Total after each pass? What does it really output?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Total is 1, then 2, then 3, then 4. It outputs <strong>4</strong>.</p><p>Line 4 sets Total back to 0 on every pass. It belongs <strong>before</strong> the loop.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">01&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Total : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">02&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">03&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR Count &larr; 1 TO 4</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">04&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &larr; 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">05&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &larr; Total + Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">06&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">07&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT Total</div></div></div><div><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px;width:100%\"><tr><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Count</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Total after the pass</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">1</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">2</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">3</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">4</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">4</td></tr></table><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>A trace table shows every value, one line at a time.</li><li>You can see the moment it goes wrong.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "activity-1",
   "label": "Activity 1: Trace and Find the Error",
   "type": "embedded-app",
   "appId": "trace-table-practice",
   "embedContainerId": "y9l26-embed-1",
