   },
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Activity 1: Trace and Find the Error</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">The trace table says 10, but the answer should be 15. Which value of Count is missing?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Count never becomes 5, so 5 is never added. The loop stops one pass too early.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Trace the program. Then answer the questions on the next slide.</p><div id=\"y9l26-embed-1\" class=\"lesson-embed\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "fix-check",
   "label": "Check: Fix the Error",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y9l26-fix-check",
   "validatorKey": "y9l26_fix_check",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Fix the Error</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Is this a syntax error or a logic error? How do you know?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>A logic error. The program runs and outputs a number, but the number is wrong.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This program should add up the numbers 1 to 5. Use your trace table.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">01&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Total : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">02&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">03&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &larr; 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">04&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR Count &larr; 1 TO 4</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">05&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &larr; Total + Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">06&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">07&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT Total</div></div></div><div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l26-fix-check-a\">(a) What does the program really output? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l26-fix-check-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"fix-check-a\" aria-label=\"Check: Fix the Error part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l26-fix-check-b\">(b) What should it output? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l26-fix-check-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"fix-check-b\" aria-label=\"Check: Fix the Error part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l26-fix-check-c\">(c) Which line has the error? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l26-fix-check-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"fix-check-c\" aria-label=\"Check: Fix the Error part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response is-line\"><label for=\"y9l26-fix-check-d\">(d) Write the correct line. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l26-fix-check-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"fix-check-d\" aria-label=\"Check: Fix the Error part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9l26-fix-check-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y9l26-fix-check-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "compare-boundary",
   "label": "Compare: More Than, or More Than or Equal?",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Compare: More Than, or More Than or Equal?</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">The pass mark is 50 or more. Mark is 50. Predict what A and B output. Which one has a logic error?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p><strong>A</strong> outputs <strong>Fail</strong>: 50 is not more than 50.</p><p><strong>B</strong> outputs <strong>Pass</strong>: 50 is equal to 50. A has the logic error.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">A</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Mark &larr; 50</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">IF Mark &gt; 50 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Pass\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Fail\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ENDIF</div></div></div><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">B</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Mark &larr; 50</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">IF Mark &gt;= 50 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Pass\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Fail\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ENDIF</div></div></div></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>&gt; means more than. &gt;= means more than <strong>or equal to</strong>.</li><li>Test the edge: always try the value that is exactly on the boundary, here 50.</li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "id": "exam-runners",
   "label": "Exam Question: Find the Errors",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y9l26-exam-runners",
   "validatorKey": "y9l26_exam_runners",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Find the Errors</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is a wrong data type a problem, even if the program runs?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>A time in a STRING is text. You cannot add times up or compare them as numbers.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Adapted from Cambridge IGCSE 0478/23, May/June 2026, Question 4(a). This algorithm should input the name and the finish time, in whole seconds, of 250 runners and store them in the arrays Runners and Times. It has three errors.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">01&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Runners : ARRAY[1:250] OF STRING</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">02&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Times : ARRAY[1:250] OF INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">03&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE RunName : STRING</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">04&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE RunTime : STRING</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">05&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Index : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">06&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR Index &larr; 1 TO 250</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">07&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT RunName</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">08&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT RunTime</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">09&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Runners[Index] &larr; RunTime</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">10&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Times[Index] &larr; RunTime</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">11&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Index</div></div></div><div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l26-exam-runners-a\">(a) Line 4: write the correct data type for RunTime. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l26-exam-runners-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-runners-a\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Find the Errors part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l26-exam-runners-b\">(b) Line 8: write the keyword that should replace OUTPUT. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l26-exam-runners-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-runners-b\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Find the Errors part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l26-exam-runners-c\">(c) Line 9: write the variable that should be stored in Runners[Index]. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l26-exam-runners-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-runners-c\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Find the Errors part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9l26-exam-runners-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y9l26-exam-runners-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "activity-2",
   "label": "Activity 2: Fix the Program",
   "type": "embedded-app",
   "appId": "drill-y9-2-6-code",
